    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>}</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></math> be defined by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be given as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Then, the sum of all the values&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> for which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> is equal to"
